  "ambiguities": [
    "FUNDING-vs-FILL SAME-INSTANT ORDER (design-basis note 2): I adopted funding-FIRST (funding settles on the position carried into the stamp, then the bar-open fill). This makes the 16:00 +cap print hit the 1.0x LONG carried in -> long PAYS +26507730 micro (cum_funding). Under the alternative fill-FIRST rule, the flip to -1.4 BTC short happens first and the short RECEIVES the cap: funding = -39606000 micro (short receives), flipping the sign and changing bar 9 cash/NAV by ~66M micro downstream. The 08:00 print is ~0 either way (rate 0.01% on a flat/fresh position). Must be reconciled before freeze.",
    "LIQUIDATION CLOSE PRICE (variant): protocol says 'force-close at the conservative side of the bar' + MATH-3 'incl. gap-through'. I used close_px = mark low 660000 (the conservative extreme, full gap-through) -> realized price loss -7831500000. Alternative reading 'close at the liquidation price 720361' gives realized loss = 230000000*(720361-1000500)/10000 = -6443197000 and final NAV ~3.39B micro instead of 2.006B. Large impact; needs an explicit rule. (Loss under either reading stays within the 9204.6 USDT allocated margin, so the isolated-margin cap does not bind.)",
    "LIQUIDATION PENALTY BASIS: I used 1% of notional at the CLOSE price (660000) = 151800000 micro. Alternatives: 1% of notional at liq price 720361 = 165683030; 1% of entry notional = 230115000. Choice shifts final NAV by up to ~78M micro.",
    "LIQUIDATION FEES: I assumed the forced close charges the liquidation penalty ONLY (no separate taker fee), consistent with IC-4 LiquidationTriggered payload (penalty_micro/loss_micro, no fee field). If a taker fee is also charged on the forced close, subtract an additional ~6.8M micro (at close 660000).",
    "ORDER SIZING REFERENCE & NAV BASIS: target_notional = target_lev x NAV, qty sized at the DECISION-BAR mark/trade close c_k (equal at all decision points), rounded toward zero to qty_step. For t8 the sizing NAV is the POST-funding equity (8814821260) because funding settled first at that instant; a pre-funding NAV (8841328990) would round to the same 1.4 BTC here, but the rule should be pinned. Sizing at the reference price (not fill price) is why realized leverage lands below target (2.3x vs 2.5x at t2, ~1.4 BTC short vs 1.5x at t8).",
    "MARGIN_USED BASIS: reported as entry_notional / |target_lev| (isolated allocation per design-basis note 1). At 2x (bars 1-2) this is 10005000000 micro, slightly ABOVE NAV (~10000 USDT) because the position was sized at reference 1000000 but filled at 1000500 (+half-spread) -> ~2.0x nominal on a marginally stale size. This is an informational field only; it does not affect cash/NAV/liquidation (maintenance margin is far away). Flag if margin_used should instead track current-mark notional or free equity.",
    "LIQUIDATION-PRICE FORMULA: used maintenance-margin crossing P_liq_long = E*(1-1/lev)/(1-maint_rate), P_liq_short = E*(1+1/lev)/(1+maint_rate), with maint_rate = 16666667e-8, agent-adverse rounding (ceil for longs, floor for shorts). Design-basis note 1 flags a ~1% shift IF the 1% penalty enters the liq-price formula; I did NOT include the penalty in the trigger price. Does not affect the variant trigger (660000 << 720361 under all readings) but shifts the reported near-liq distance at bar 5 (currently min_intrabar 3307248 = ~3.31%).",
    "METRIC ROUNDING DIRECTION: net_return_1e8 reported with FLOOR rounding (-9664508 main; -79936552 variant). If the estimator truncates toward zero instead, main is -9664507. Spec text says floor; pinned here as floor.",
